#: resources/views/admin.phtml:318
msgid "Pseudo-Events (state polling)"
msgstr ""

#: resources/views/admin.phtml:320
msgid ""
"webtrees has no event bus, so core actions are observed by polling. The "
"module checks the states below at most every 5 minutes and queues an event "
"when something changes; an event-triggered job then acts on it. The first "
"run only records a baseline and does not fire."
msgstr ""

#: resources/views/admin.phtml:321
msgid ""
"To activate, enable the \"cronjob:pseudo-events\" job in the table above. It "
"runs in the tick child process - isolated from any web request and bounded "
"by its timeout."
msgstr ""

#: resources/views/admin.phtml:326
msgid "Route events (request-triggered)"
msgstr ""

#: resources/views/admin.phtml:328
msgid ""
"Detects mutations directly from their HTTP route (e.g. a note edit) and "
"queues a matching event immediately - in addition to the polling pseudo-"
"events above. Only curated routes fire, only while this is enabled AND a "
"matching event job is listening."
msgstr ""

#: resources/views/admin.phtml:337
msgid "Disable route events"
msgstr ""

#: resources/views/admin.phtml:337
msgid "Enable route events"
msgstr ""

#: resources/views/admin.phtml:344
msgid "Event webhook (external trigger)"
msgstr ""

#: resources/views/admin.phtml:347
msgid ""
"External systems can queue an event by GETting the endpoint below. Each "
"queued event runs its matching event-triggered job(s) at the next tick. The "
"token is required (send it in the X-Cronjob-Token header, not in the URL) "
"and the endpoint is rate-limited."
msgstr ""

#: resources/views/admin.phtml:355
msgid "Endpoint"
msgstr ""

#: resources/views/admin.phtml:360
msgid ""
"GET with query params event=<name> and data=<json> (optional); send the "
"token in the X-Cronjob-Token header (never in the URL - it would end up in "
"access logs)."
msgstr ""

